  "voting_summary": "California mails every registered voter a ballot, and 78% of its 2024 vote came by mail, with ballots postmarked by election day accepted for a week afterward. Most in-person voting happens at vote centers open up to 11 days, reported as a single in-person total rather than split by day. Polls close at 11 p.m. Eastern; pre-processed mail is released first, in-person ballots follow overnight, and late mail is verified in batches over the following weeks. Mail ran D+27 versus R+5 for in-person, so the state drifts steadily bluer through the canvass.",
